  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EBRD ETC MEI Fund</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EBRD ETC MEI Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen omfattar st&#xf6;d till en fond p&#xe5; EBRD - Early Transition        Countries Municipal and Environmental Infrastructure. M&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att    minska milj&#xf6;f&#xf6;roreningar och f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra naturresursanv&#xe4;ndningen,       framf&#xf6;rallt inom kommunal milj&#xf6;infrastuktur.Fonden anv&#xe4;nds f&#xf6;r        f&#xf6;rberedande studier och reformst&#xf6;d. Under fonden ges st&#xf6;d till ett   flertal projekt, framf&#xf6;rallt i &#xd6;steuropa.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is to promote the sustainable   use of natural resources and protection of the environment in the     Early Transition Countries. This will be done through the             establishment of a Municipal Environmental Infrastructure (MEI) fund  that supports the EBRD with resources for consultancy and technical   assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The fund objective is to finance&#xa0; advisory services and technical assistance for municipal environment infrastructure projects financed by EBRD and/or Sida related to EBRD&apos;s ETC initiative, with the aim of supporting environmentally, financially and socially sustainable projects. The objective was later extended to also include investment grant financing of such projects. In an effort to reduce number of trust funds between Sida and EBRD, the fund&#xa0;was merged with two other trust funds of similar purpose.</narrative>
  </description>
